  "title": "Mary Wollstonecraft",
  "summary": "Born on 27 April 1759 in Spitalfields, London, Wollstonecraft published A Vindication of the Rights of Men in 1790 and A Vindication of the Rights of Woman in 1792, both with the London publisher Joseph Johnson. She travelled to France in December 1792 and died in 1797 after childbirth. The pin marks London, where she was born and published.",
